          ],
          "attribution": "source",
          "importance": "core",
          "attribution_start": null,
          "attribution_end": null
        },
        {
          "id": "F4_2",
          "source_id": "part4",
          "source_sha256": "4b39a681477033568d0a210e045c427d350a832531670400d754cfc99f9a0096",
          "start": 24780,
          "end": 25372,
          "quote": "There are actually\ntwo types of objects.\nOne are scalar objects.\nThat means these are very basic\nobjects in Python from which\neverything can be made.\nThese are scalar objects.\nThat can't be subdivided.\nThe other type of object\nis a non-scalar object.\nAnd these are objects that\nhave some internal structure.\nFor example, the\nnumber five is a scalar\nobject because it\ncan't be subdivided.\nBut a list of numbers,\nfor example, 5, 6,\n7,8, is going to be\na non-scalar object\nbecause you can subdivide it.\nYou can subdivide it into--\nyou can find parts to it.\nIt's made up of a\nsequence of numbers.",
          "topic": "标量对象与非标量对象",
          "claim": "Python对象分为标量对象和非标量对象：标量对象是基本对象，不可再分；非标量对象具有内部结构，可再分。例如数字5是标量对象，而列表[5,6,7,8]是非标量对象。",
