          "attribution_start": null,
          "attribution_end": null
        },
        {
          "id": "F2_8",
          "source_id": "part2",
          "source_sha256": "f93de099f8cbf3578a6ca1fa84294bfe67a979103d1d34f4aa33ddcd9791eda3",
          "start": 12995,
          "end": 13278,
          "quote": "This recipe is there\nfor an algorithm.\nIn computer science speak,\nit's going to be an algorithm.\nAnd that's what we're going\nto learn about in this class.\nWe're dealing with computers.\nAnd we actually want\nto capture a recipe\ninside a computer, a computer\nbeing a mechanical process.",
          "topic": "算法与课程主题",
          "claim": "在计算机科学术语中，这种配方就是算法，这也是本课程将要学习的内容；课程涉及计算机，并希望将配方捕获到计算机这一机械过程中。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            225,
            226,
            227,
            228,
            229,
            230,
            231,
            232,
            233,
            234,
            235
          ],
          "attribution": "source",
          "importance": "core",
          "attribution_start": null,
          "attribution_end": null
        },
        {
          "id": "F2_9",
          "source_id": "part2",
          "source_sha256": "f93de099f8cbf3578a6ca1fa84294bfe67a979103d1d34f4aa33ddcd9791eda3",
          "start": 13279,
          "end": 14061,
          "quote": "Historically, there were two\ndifferent types of computers.\nOriginally, there\nwere these things\ncalled fixed-program computers.\nAnd I'm old enough to\nhave used something\nlike this, where there's\njust numbers and plus, minus,\nmultiplication,\ndivide, and equal.\nBut calculators these days\nare a lot more complicated.\nBut way back then, an example\nof a fixed-program computer\nis this calculator.\nIt only knows how to do\naddition, multiplication,\nsubtraction, division.\nIf you want to plot\nsomething, you can't.\nIf you want to go on the\ninternet, send email with it,\nyou can't.\nIt can only do this one thing.\nAnd if you wanted to create a\nmachine that did another thing,\nthen you'd have to create\nanother fixed-program computer\nthat did a completely\nseparate test.\nThat's not very great.",
          "topic": "固定程序计算机及其局限",
          "claim": "历史上最初有固定程序计算机，例如只懂加、减、乘、除的旧式计算器；它只能做这一件事，不能绘图、上网或发邮件，若要执行另一项任务就必须制造另一台完全独立的固定程序计算机。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            236,
            237,
            238,
            239,
            240,
            241,
            242,
            243,
            244,
            245,
            246,
