          ],
          "attribution": "source",
          "importance": "core",
          "attribution_start": null,
          "attribution_end": null
        },
        {
          "id": "F3_5",
          "source_id": "part3",
          "source_sha256": "6d79f62fb65eec01763882639740143b58a04805503a24b5660d4dfa475079d9",
          "start": 18061,
          "end": 18371,
          "quote": "Once you have your\nset of primitives\nfor a particular language, you\ncan start creating expressions.\nAnd these expressions\nare going to be\ncombinations of the primitives\nin the programming language.\nAnd the expressions are\ngoing to have some value.\nAnd they're going up some\nmeaning in the programming\nlanguage.",
          "topic": "表达式与原语的组合",
          "claim": "一旦有了某种语言的原语集合，就可以开始创建表达式；表达式是编程语言中原语的组合，会具有某个值，并在编程语言中具有某种含义。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            88,
            89,
            90,
            91,
            92,
            93,
            94,
            95,
            96,
            97,
            98,
            99,
            100
          ],
          "attribution": "source",
          "importance": "core",
          "attribution_start": null,
          "attribution_end": null
        },
        {
          "id": "F3_6",
          "source_id": "part3",
          "source_sha256": "6d79f62fb65eec01763882639740143b58a04805503a24b5660d4dfa475079d9",
          "start": 18372,
          "end": 19403,
          "quote": "Let's do a little bit of\na parallel with English\njust so you see what I mean.\nIn English, the\nprimitive constructs\nare going to be words.\nThere's a lot of words\nin the English language.\nProgramming languages-- in\nPython, there are primitives,\nbut there aren't\nas many of them.\nThere are floats,\nBooleans, these\nare numbers, strings,\nand simple operators,\nlike addition,\nsubtraction, and so on.\nSo we have primitive constructs.\nUsing these\nprimitive constructs,\nwe can start creating, in\nEnglish, phrases, sentences,\nand the same in\nprogramming languages.\nIn English, we can say\nsomething like, \"cat, dog, boy.\nThat, we say, is not\nsyntactically valid.\nThat's bad syntax.\nThat's noun, noun, noun.\nThat doesn't make sense.\nWhat does have good syntax in\nEnglish is noun, verb, noun.\nSo, \"cat, hugs boy\" is\nSimilarly, in a\nprogramming language,\nsomething like this-- in\nPython, in this case-- a word\nand then the number five\ndoesn't really make sense.\nIt's not syntactically valid.\nBut something like operator,\noperand, operator is OK.",
          "topic": "英语与编程语言的原语和语法对比",
          "claim": "在英语中，原始构造是单词，数量很多；在Python中，原语包括浮点数、布尔值、数字、字符串以及加法、减法等简单运算符，数量没有那么多。使用这些原始构造，在英语和编程语言中都可以开始创建短语、句子；例如英语中“cat, dog, boy”是名词、名词、名词，语法无效，而名词、动词、名词（如“cat hugs boy”）具有良好语法；类似地，在Python中，一个单词后跟数字5没有意义、语法无效，而运算符、操作数、运算符是可以的。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            101,
