          ],
          "attribution": "source",
          "importance": "core",
          "attribution_start": null,
          "attribution_end": null
        },
        {
          "id": "F3_2",
          "source_id": "part3",
          "source_sha256": "6d79f62fb65eec01763882639740143b58a04805503a24b5660d4dfa475079d9",
          "start": 16571,
          "end": 17085,
          "quote": "Just to recap, you have\nthe stored program computer\nthat contains these\nsequences of instructions.\nThe primitive operations\nthat it can do\nare addition, subtraction,\nlogic operations, tests--\nwhich are something equal\nto something else, something\nless than, and so\non-- and moving data,\nso storing data, moving data\naround, and things like that.\nAnd the interpreter goes\nthrough every instruction\nand decides whether you're going\nto go to the next instruction,\nskip instructions, or repeat\ninstructions, and so on.",
          "topic": "存储程序计算机的原始操作与解释器",
          "claim": "存储程序计算机包含指令序列，其原始操作包括加法、减法、逻辑运算、测试（如相等、小于等）以及移动数据（存储数据、移动数据等）；解释器遍历每条指令，决定是进入下一条指令、跳过指令还是重复指令等。",
          "evidence_indices": [
            27,
